            <ArticleTitle>[Effects of fermented Cordyceps powder on pulmonary function in sensitized guinea pigs and airway inflammation in sensitized rats].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>622-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To study Cordyceps (artificial fermented Cordyceps sinensis(Berk.) Sacc) powderin the treatment of asthma in the animal models.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHOD" NlmCategory="METHODS">Pulmonary function and airway inflammation in vivo were investigated.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULT" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Cordyceps, 5g.kg-1(ig), significantly inhibited bronchial challenge of ovalbumin-induced change of RL and Cdyn (P &lt; 0.05) and inhibited antigen-induced increase of eosinophils in the BALF of rats (P &lt; 0.05).</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">The results suggested cordyceps could be applied for the prevention and cure of asthma.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
